# UI — out-of-the-box first

Default strategy for any UX/UI work: **use existing, battle-tested components**. Custom UI increases a11y, keyboard, and cross-browser testing load. Build from scratch only when no suitable free library exists.

## Before writing UI

1. Check `apps/web/components/ui/` (shadcn/Radix wrappers already in repo).
2. Check installed deps: Radix, cmdk, match-sorter, sonner, react-day-picker, lucide-react.
3. Search [shadcn/ui](https://ui.shadcn.com) for the pattern (Combobox, Select, Command, etc.).
4. Prefer adding a shadcn component via its standard Radix wrapper over hand-rolling HTML.

## Use these (already in stack)

| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| Buttons, cards, inputs | `@/components/ui/*` |
| Dialogs, popovers, dropdowns | Radix via `@/components/ui/dialog`, `popover`, `dropdown-menu` |
| Select / combobox | `@/components/ui/select`, `command` + `popover` |
| Search / filter lists | `match-sorter` + cmdk `shouldFilter={false}` |
| Checkboxes, radios | `@/components/ui/checkbox`, `radio-group` |
| Dates | `date-field` → `calendar` (react-day-picker) |
| Toasts | `sonner` via `@/components/ui/sonner` |
| Icons | `lucide-react` |
| Client state | `zustand` (not custom event buses) |

## Do not

- Raw `<select>`, `<input type="checkbox">`, `<input type="radio">` when Radix/shadcn equivalents exist.
- Import `cmdk` directly — use `@/components/ui/command`.
- Custom fuzzy search / Levenshtein — use `match-sorter` or cmdk filtering.
- Custom modal/focus-trap/dropdown logic — use Radix primitives.

## Custom UI is OK for

- Product-specific layouts (timelines, wizards, dashboards).
- Domain components that **compose** OOTB primitives (`vehicle-ymm-picker`, `onboarding-wizard`).

## When no OOTB fit exists

Document in the PR why (e.g. "no Radix equivalent for X") and add focused tests for the custom behavior.
